  "slug": "consortium-2026-0b54",
  "summary": "Updated 2026 resources and the HUPO 2025 proteome report expand reference coverage, standardized reprocessing, and open proteomics data access.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is the maintenance of shared proteomics infrastructure: reference proteome annotation, reprocessed abundance compendia, and open data standards. The HUPO HPP 2025 report places 19,435 proteins in the reference proteome, with 93.6% detected and 5,562 proteins now carrying FE1 function-level assignments. PaxDb v6.0 reprocesses 1639 public MS datasets from 392 species through a standardized FragPipe pipeline, adding metadata, orthology mappings, and LLM-assisted curation. The ProteomeXchange consortium frames its 2026 contribution around making proteomics data FAIR, while Expression Atlas 2026 reports over 4500 studies across 67 species with expanded proteomics content. A spotted hyena study is less directly aligned: it benchmarks three draft genomes and a Trinity transcriptome for database searches, with 2022-Shao performing best, which bears on database construction for non-model organisms.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-01-11"
}
